# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ - generated caches vs. curated seed data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Almost everything in data/ is DERIVED, disposable data: delete it and
# `scripts/bootstrap.sh` puts it back from public, unauthenticated sources.
# Committing those caches would ship a stale copy of the internet, so the rule
# is "ignore data/ by default, then allow back the handful of hand-maintained
# files that bootstrap.sh never overwrites".
#
# NOTE: git has no trailing comments in .gitignore, so every note here is on
# its own line. Order matters - the last matching pattern wins.
data/*

# --- curated seed data that MUST ship -------------------------------------
# hand-tuned per-registry concurrency budgets (sweep.sh)
!data/registry-limits.tsv
# hand-maintained RDAP / whois escape hatch (lib.sh reads it first)
!data/rdap-overrides.tsv
# reputation seeds, canonical file; bootstrap.sh only ever appends
!data/tld-flags.tsv
# short alias: symlink -> tld-flags.tsv
!data/reputation.tsv
!data/.gitkeep

# --- generated caches ------------------------------------------------------
# Already covered by `data/*`, but listed by name so the intent survives any
# future loosening of that rule:
#   rdap-bootstrap.json   raw IANA RDAP bootstrap
#   rdap-endpoints.tsv    built RDAP index          (alias tldmap.tsv)
#   porkbun-pricing.json  raw Porkbun price list
#   tld-prices.tsv        built price table         (alias prices.tsv)
#   whois-servers.tsv     seeded, then grown lazily from whois.iana.org
data/rdap-bootstrap.json
data/rdap-endpoints.tsv
data/tldmap.tsv
data/porkbun-pricing.json
data/tld-prices.tsv
data/prices.tsv
data/whois-servers.tsv

# Half-written downloads and rebuilds (bootstrap.sh stages into temp files).
*.tmp
*.new
*.part
*.partial
*.download

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch, scratchpads and local run output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
scratchpad/
scratchpads/
tmp/
out/
results/
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.#*
*.sw?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials - nothing resembling a secret goes near a commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# quote.sh reads PORKBUN_API_KEY / PORKBUN_SECRET_KEY from the environment.
# Keep them in a local .env or your shell profile, never in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
.netrc
.htpasswd
credentials
credentials.*
secrets
secrets.*
*secret*
*.token
*_token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
